# The justfile in this repository is lowercase, so canon's `Justfile` rule does
# not match it on a case-sensitive filesystem.
justfile text eol=lf

# ── WHY THE RETIRED `server/mix.lock` LINE IS GONE ──────────────────────────
# This file carried `server/mix.lock text eol=lf -diff` until 2026-09-27. Issue
# #74 retired this repository's own Elixir relay in favour of the external
# metadatastician/burble fabric (ADR-0006) and the `server/` tree went with it.
# No `.ex`, `.exs`, or `mix.lock` file is tracked here any more, so the line
# matched nothing. Canon's unqualified `mix.lock` rule above covers the file if
# an Elixir tree ever returns, which is strictly better than a path-scoped rule
# that silently stops applying the moment the path is renamed.

# ── GAME ASSET TYPES ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This repository is a game. Its `source/` tree is text-first by design (see
# source/README.md: authored content is human-readable and diffable, and
# `assets/` holds the Bevy-loadable artefacts generated from it), but the
# finished game will carry audio, video, textures, meshes, and fonts. Declaring
# them NOW means the first real asset lands with the right eol/binary treatment
# instead of being normalised to LF on the way in and corrupted.
#
# Every type below is one Bevy 0.17 can load, or one a documented authoring
# pipeline produces. Nothing speculative.

# Audio. Bevy loads ogg, wav, mp3, flac natively (bevy_audio / kira).
*.ogg   binary
*.opus  binary
*.wav   binary
*.flac  binary
*.mp3   binary
*.aiff  binary
*.m4a   binary
*.xm    binary
*.mod   binary
*.s3m   binary
*.it    binary

# Video / cutscene containers. Bevy has no first-party video decoder; these are
# declared because source/video/ holds authored cutscene inputs and the
# pipeline document records how they become frames or an external player call.
*.mp4   binary
*.webm  binary
*.mov   binary
*.mkv   binary
*.avi   binary

# Textures and compressed GPU formats. ktx2/basis are Bevy's preferred runtime
# formats; the rest are authoring inputs.
*.ktx2  binary
*.basis binary
*.dds   binary
*.tga   binary
*.bmp   binary
*.tif   binary
*.tiff  binary
*.psd   binary
*.xcf   binary
*.ase   binary
*.aseprite binary

# Meshes, scenes, and animation. glTF is Bevy's runtime format; the others are
# authoring inputs that the pipeline converts.
*.gltf  text eol=lf
*.glb   binary
*.fbx   binary
*.obj   text eol=lf
*.mtl   text eol=lf
*.blend binary
*.dae   text eol=lf

# Fonts. Bevy loads ttf/otf; canon already declares woff/woff2/ttf/otf binary.
*.fon   binary

# Shaders. WGSL is text and Bevy loads it directly; SPIR-V is the compiled form.
*.wgsl  text eol=lf
*.spv   binary

# ── GENERATED ARTEFACTS: suppressed diffs, excluded from language stats ─────
# `assets/` is derived from `source/` and is reproducible. Marking it generated
# keeps a regeneration commit from showing as a 40 000-line diff in review and
# keeps GitHub's primary-language badge measuring the code that is actually
# written here.
assets/**           linguist-generated=true
assets/**  -diff

# The lockfile that decides which GitHub Action revisions run. It IS source
# (hand-corrected, see scripts/check-lock-sync.sh), so unlike Cargo.lock it is
# deliberately NOT marked -diff: a reviewer must see exactly which ref moved.
.github/workflows/actions.lock text eol=lf

# ── GIT LFS: DELIBERATELY NOT CONFIGURED ────────────────────────────────────
# No `filter=lfs` attribute appears anywhere in this file. That is a decision,
# not an omission: git-lfs is not installed in this repository's development
# environment, and an lfs filter in .gitattributes makes a plain `git clone`
# produce pointer files instead of content for anyone without the client. That
# failure is silent and confusing.
#
# Today the repository tracks zero binary assets, so the question is not yet
# live. It becomes live the first time a real texture, sound, or cutscene lands.
# The trade-off is recorded as an open owner ruling in
# docs/decisions-pending/DR-0003-asset-storage-and-lfs.md rather than being
# decided here unilaterally.
